The '''Yangwang U9''' ({{Lang-zh|c=仰望U9|p=Yǎngwàng U9|l=Looking up towards U9}}) is a [[battery electric car|battery electric]] [[supercar|super]]-[[coupe]] manufactured by [[BYD Auto]] under its [[luxury car]] brand [[Yangwang]]. The U9 is the second vehicle from the Yangwang brand after the [[Yangwang U8|U8]] [[off-road vehicle|off-road]] [[SUV]], and was formally introduced on [[Auto Shanghai]] in April 2023. As of April 2026, its "Xtreme" variant has been excluded from the list of the [[List of production car speed records#Cars excluded from the list|fastest production car in the world]] due to the car only being tested one way rather than both ways, with a top speed of {{convert|496|km/h|mi/h}}.

==Overview==
The U9 was developed by German car designer [[Wolfgang Egger]], who previously served as a head designer for [[Alfa Romeo]], [[Audi]] and [[Lamborghini]], and began working for BYD in 2017.<ref>{{Cite web |date=January 5, 2023 |title=YangWang U9 Is A $145,000 Electric Supercar From China That Hits 60 In 2.0 Sec |url=https://www.carscoops.com/2023/01/byds-yangwang-u9-is-another-electric-supercar-from-china/ |website=Carscoops}}</ref>

The U9 was first introduced on 6 April 2023, and went on sale in February 2024.<ref name="CNC" /> Mass production officially started on 16 August 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-08-17 |title=仰望U9首台车下线 将陆续开启交付 |trans-title=The first Yangwang U9 car rolled off the assembly line and will be delivered in succession |url=https://www.autohome.com.cn/fastmessage/detail/1299579.html#pvareaid=6849221 |access-date=2024-08-17 |website=www.autohome.com.cn}}</ref>

The U9 achieved an uncertified [[Nürburgring Nordschleife]] lap time of 7 minutes and 17.9 seconds in November 2024. It also achieved a straight-line top speed of {{convert|391.94|km/h|mph|abbr=on}}, making it the fastest Chinese car in serial production.<ref>{{cite news |last=Pappas |first=Thanos |date=2024-11-13 |title=YangWang U9 Hits 244 MPH Top Speed, But Can’t Beat The Taycan At The Nurburgring |url=https://www.carscoops.com/2024/11/yangwang-u9-ev-hits-244-mph-top-speed-but-fails-to-impress-at-the-nurburgring/ |website=Carscoops |publisher=Carscoops |location=US |access-date=2024-11-15}}</ref>

